                        <summary/>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i1">               
                            <locus from="1r" to="74r"/>
                            <title>History of Ethiopia and the Catholics</title>
                            <note>Collection of historical accounts by <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS12520TaklaH">Takla Hāymanot</persName> regarding the political and religious 
                                history of Eritrea and the Ethiopian Highlands. It relies primarily on traditional sources such as chronological lists and 
                                the <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2375Synaxa">Sǝnkǝsār (General record)</ref>, yet displays a greater degree of originality from the reign of
                                <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS10303Yekunno">Yǝkunno ʾAmlāk</persName> (from <locus target="#21v"/>) onwards and becomes more detailed for the 
                                period starting in the <date notBefore="1820" notAfter="1829">1820ies</date> (from <locus target="25r"/>). The 
                                historical accounts end with the suicide of  <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS9430Tewodros">Tewodros II</persName> at <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC4547Maqdal">Maqdalā</placeName>
                                in <date when="1868">1868</date>. The text is divided into 31 chapters of varying lengths, the beginnings of which are
                                not marked in the first ten chapters. A large part of the narrative on <locus from="25r" to="74r"/> deals with the life story
                                of <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS3451DeJacob">Giustino De Jacobis</persName>, whom the author knew well. A considerable number of the details presented 
                                in this document were set forth by this missionary in <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/ZGKTT8NI"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:TaklaHaymanot1914Jacobis"/><title level="m">Abouna Yacob; ou, Le vénérable de Jacobis. Scènes de sa vie d'apostolat, racontées par un témoin.</title><author><t:name xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">Takla Hāymānot</t:name></author><pubPlace>Paris</pubPlace><publisher>En vente: à la procure des Lazaristes</publisher><date>1914</date></bibl>.  
                                See also <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT5354Mashaf">Maṣḥafa ʾaḫgʷǝlota ḥassat</ref> in <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ANLcr79">Rome, Biblioteca dell’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei, Conti Rossini 79</ref> by the same author.
                                For the larger part of the treatise from <locus from="19v1" to="74r"/>, an Italian translation was published by 
                                <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS3182ContiRo">
                  Carlo
                  Conti Rossini
               </persName> in <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/9AVKHNEC"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:ContiRossini1916Fonti"/><title level="a">Fonti storiche etiopiche per il secolo XIX. I. Vicende dell’Etiopia e delle missioni cattoliche ai tempi di ras Ali, deggiac Ubiè e re Teodoro secondo un documento abissino</title><title level="j">Atti della Reale Accademia dei Lincei, Rendiconti, Classe di scienze morale, storiche e filologiche</title><title level="s">sér. V</title><author><t:forename xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">Carlo</t:forename><t:surname xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">Conti Rossini</t:surname></author><date>1916</date><series><t:title xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" level="s">sér. V</t:title></series><biblScope unit="volume">25</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">425–550</biblScope></bibl>. In the preface to
                                this translation on page 425 to 427, there is a description of this document and its author.</note>
